WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.000
If you want to hear how the next Stephen King
remake may be teased at the end of It: Chapter

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.540
2, then stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.099
Welcome to Things You Missed, I am traveling
this week so I’m not in the studio, but

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:18.170
I did get my own copy of It Chapter 2, so
I scrubbed through it and found, surprisingly,

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.710
a lot more that I hadn’t caught in theaters.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.300
So if you haven’t seen my original 71 Things
You Missed, I’d recommend you watch that

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.760
one first, but assuming you have seen it,
let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.140
[THINGS YOU MISSED]

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.610
One thing I brought up when covering the first
It was the constant cosmic references that

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.360
set up Pennywise’s origins from outer space
in the second movie, and I did notice some

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.270
teases in the second chapter as well.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.850
The Ferris Wheel at the Festival is called
the Astro, the carnival mural features sun

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.620
and moon paintings and we can see that Eddie’s
phone is a Galaxy S8.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.580
This all ties into the Ritual of Chud, which
they eventually use to try to defeat It.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.480
In the novel, the backstory is expanded and
we learn about the ancient rivalry between

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.400
It, and it’s rival, Maturin the Turtle.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.080
I pointed out some references to the Turtle
in the last video, but I found even more,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.270
such as this one in Henry’s room at the
asylum.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:04.910
Mike also speaks of a root that the native
americans believed has mystic properties,

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:08.320
which he also puts in Bill’s drink so that
he too can see the Ritual of Chud.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.120
Roll it.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.000
"Their holy man.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.900
Their holy of holies.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.780
He took me in.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.640
Fed me their sacred Maturin.”

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.920
The turtle isn’t refered to as Maturin in
the novel It, but we learn of the name Maturin

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.570
and more lore in Stephen King’s Dark Tower
series.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:32.340
We first meet adult Bill on the set of the
movie he’s adapting from his own novel,

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.340
Attic Room.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.600
If you pause here you can get a better look
at the book version, and it’s massive, much

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.180
like the novel It, and there’s a forward
by someone named Jason Ballantine.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.130
When we later see the copy of his other book,
The Black Rapids, Jason Ballantine is also

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.310
responsible for the forward.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.460
This is a reference to the editor of both
It and It Chapter 2.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.530
Usually when we see a crew member referenced like that,
the art department makes references to themselves,

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.350
so I think it’s nice that the editor got
some love in this one.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.201
This next part is something that I did notice
in the theaters, but I almost couldn’t believe

00:01:58.201 --> 00:02:01.910
my own eyes, and ultimately just thought I
must have imagined it, and thus didn’t put

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:03.390
it the previous episode.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.530
So the movie they are shooting is called Attic
Room at Warner Bros studios, but on this camera

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.250
tape, the memo doesn’t say Attic Room, it
says, Attic Panic.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.700
But what is Attic Panic?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.300
Well, It Chapter 2 takes place in 2016, and
one big horror movie that Warner Bros released

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:21.090
in 2016 is Lights Out, directed by David Sandberg,
who was hired after posting his short film

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.980
Lights Out to YouTube and it being massively
successful.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.400
One of his other shorts on his YouTube channel
is called Attic Panic.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.700
If you’ve seen my episode on Annabelle:
Creation, you know that many of the concepts

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.640
from Attic Panic made it into Annabelle: Creation
as well, which of course, is made by Warner

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.640
Bros.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.069
The date on this label is 10/10/2018, which
is obviously impossible since the film takes

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:43.020
place in 2016, but probably is just a fun
little reference to the day this scene of

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.680
IT was actually shot, since we can literally
see it says IT 2 right here.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.310
I’ve also already pointed out this cameo
by Peter Bogdonovich, but not the fact that

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.970
he’s wearing a VISTOW pin.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.910
Vistow stands for Volunteers In Service To
Orson Welles a reference to another movie

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.700
where Bogdonovich plays a director.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.060
When Mike calls up the other losers, his area
code is from Bangor, Maine.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.190
The novel It was written in Bangor, and it’s
said to serve as an inspiration for many of

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.970
the locations in Derry, and speaking of Derry,
when Richie is about to go on stage at the

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.260
comedy club, a poster in the background says
“Home We Go” foreshadowing the homecoming

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.190
that the Losers Club would soon face.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.730
The next one we meet is Ben, and one of his
employees in the board meeting is played by

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.880
Brandon Crane, the very same Brandon Crane
who played the 12 year old Ben Hanscom in

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.520
the original 1990 adaptation of It.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.660
After being introduced to the adult Losers
Club, there’s one more adult version we

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:29.660
meet.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.590
Other than Greta Keene, I guess.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:35.400
I’m talking about Henry Bowers, who is locked
up in Juniper Hills Mental Hospital, where

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.360
some of the other patients are watching an
episode of Tom and Jerry.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.530
This particular clip shows a piece of meat
going down into the sewers, just Derry’s children

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.879
are food that is lured into the sewer system
by Pennywise.

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:49.500
One of the new aspects of Richie’s character
in Chapter 2 is the fact that he is revealed

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.780
to be bi-sexual.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.760
There are actually some hints about this early
on.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.810
At the Chinese restaurant, he asks Eddie if
he’s married, before clarifying, “What? To a

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:57.810
woman?”

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.000
Then he addresses Ben’s weightloss.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.160
"Wait, let's talk about the elephant not in the room.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.800
You're hot.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.260
You're like every Brazilian soccer player wrapped up into one person.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.680
At the end of that meal, Mike fills them all
in on It, and shows off a couple pages of

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.680
his book.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:16.579
The novel It is broken up by these interludes
written by Mike that provide exposition about

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:18.139
the Derry and about the monster.

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:22.059
The film offers little glimpses of details
about It, like this page that discusses Le

00:04:22.059 --> 00:04:26.849
Loup Garou, the French werewolf slash skinchanger
that the kids discuss as they compare It to

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:30.099
legends in many other cultures in Chapter
13 of the novel.

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:33.819
We can also see some other thoughts from Mike
that I just found interesting, like him questioning

00:04:33.819 --> 00:04:37.930
if the deadlights are a hallucination, or
his plans to save up money to leave Derry

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.479
when this is all over, which he does.

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:42.770
At the end of the movie we get another look
at this book, where we see Mike describing

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:46.300
the bird form of It, which is his biggest
fear in the book, and also there’s a map

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.830
of the proximity between where Adrian Mellon
is found compared to where the lumberjacks

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.800
are found in 1879, something I discussed in
greater detail in the Pennywise Horror History.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:59.289
Back at the hotel, Ben and Beverly talk in
the bar, and one of the bottles in the background

00:04:59.289 --> 00:05:02.059
resembles a clown from the clown room in Chapter
One.

00:05:02.059 --> 00:05:05.520
And as long as I’m talking about connections
to Chapter One, you know the music that plays

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.740
during Penny’s infamous dance scene?

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.340
We can hear that again as Bill runs into the
funhouse at the Derry Canal Days Festival.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.900
I also pointed out director Andy Muschietti’s
cameo in the first video, what I didn’t

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.139
realize is what he’s browsing in the pharmacy.

00:05:39.139 --> 00:05:42.639
Like Beverly Marsh in the first movie, he’s
eyeing a box of tampons.

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:46.569
By the way, after seeing my first video on
It Chapter 2, Andy DMed me with a couple of

00:05:46.569 --> 00:05:47.560
additional easter eggs.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.080
“The little bully kid at the opening is
played by Katie LUnman, aka, Betty Ripsom

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.099
in Chapter 1”.

00:05:53.099 --> 00:05:57.250
He also hints that The Abbey Road album cover
featured Paul McCartney walking barefoot.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.360
Conspiracy theories said Paul was DEAD and
that was a signal.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.009
There’s a shot in the movie where one of
the adult losers is barefoot.

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:04.139
Who is it?

00:06:04.139 --> 00:06:08.819
The answer being Ben, did surprise me, though
technically you do see Stan’s barefoot as

00:06:08.819 --> 00:06:13.080
he gets in the tub, but he’s completely
naked, so not sure if that counts.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.620
One thing I was interested to take a closer
look at was the bathroom stall that Beverly

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.559
is thrown into for her encounter with It.

00:06:18.559 --> 00:06:22.409
Unfortunately, I wasn’t able to find a lot
of meaning in most of the graffiti, but here

00:06:22.409 --> 00:06:24.139
are the ones I found most interesting.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:29.240
The right side is all about BJs, and one of
the messages says, “BJ’s, call CLOWNS”.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.879
So take that how you will.

00:06:30.879 --> 00:06:34.629
Another says, “your father is proud of you”,
perhaps this is a mock insult about Bev’s

00:06:34.629 --> 00:06:38.550
dad, or maybe it just ties into the aforementioned
BJs, as kind of a joke.

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:42.180
Then there are what seems to be three clues
about how to defeat It.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.560
The first says, "with the lights out it's
less dangerous."

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.480
Then there's one that says, "smaller the better".

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.040
And then finally, "big is what it seems."

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:06.240
If you find anything interesting, drop me
a comment, but I'm moving on to the plethora

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.099
of references to other works.

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:11.779
The first one is this name plate at the library
which says Wendy Torrance, the name of the

00:07:11.779 --> 00:07:14.550
Mom from The Shining, which is also written
by Stephen King.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:18.539
Then in the movie theater arcade, we see the
remains of a poster for the Avengers.

00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:22.889
No, not the one you just thought of, I’m
talking about the 1998 film The Avengers.

00:07:22.889 --> 00:07:26.449
I haven’t seen the movie, so I can’t say
much more than that, but it does add weight

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:30.020
to my theory that the movie theater closed
down in the year 1998.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.840
In the junk shop that Stephen King’s character
works at there are a bunch of license plates,

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:39.099
one of which is CQB 241, the license plate
from another Stephen King story, Christine.

00:07:39.099 --> 00:07:42.840
One thing I mentioned in the last video was
a newspaper headline mentioning someone named

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.870
Gillespie, and how it may have been a reference
to cop from Stephen King’s vampire novel

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:47.870
Salem’s Lot.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:51.909
And after being able to pause and take a better
look at this text, it totally is a big reference

00:07:51.909 --> 00:07:52.909
to Salem’s Lot.

00:07:52.909 --> 00:07:56.149
The headline reads “Constable Gillespie’s
Investigation Widens”

00:07:56.149 --> 00:08:00.009
Neighboring city turmoil forces officer into
toughest decision of his career.

00:08:00.009 --> 00:08:03.879
This confirms that the events of Salem’s
Lot do take place in the nearby Jerusalem’s

00:08:03.879 --> 00:08:07.809
Lot prior to the events of It, if we’re
going by the altered timeline of the Muschietti

00:08:07.809 --> 00:08:11.309
It films and really seems to suggest that
Salem’s Lot will be the next Stephen King

00:08:11.309 --> 00:08:14.759
novel slash TV movie to get the big Hollywood
treatment.

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:16.210
And by the way, it is.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:20.330
James Wan’s name has been mentioned, as
has It Chapter 2 screenwriter Gary Dauberman.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:23.919
My last Thing You Missed of the year, is kind
of a tragic one.

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:28.009
Stan, in his final letter, the last thing
he ever writes in his life, misspelled the

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:29.040
word lose.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:33.100
"See, the thing about being a Loser is you don't have anything to lose."

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.720
Way to go out Stan.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.520
Great going.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:39.770
Check out the video on the left for the complete
history of Stan and other It Characters.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:44.410
If you love horror, remember to subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:47.240
that deathbell for notifications, and I’ll
see you next year.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.120
Assuming we both survive.

